                <pb facs="0286" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11G93/1087: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hartman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-22T09:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 22,
                                1920—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Department’s March 19, 6 p.m. Daily deposits do not amount to one three
                    hundred sixty fifth of total annual amount due on railroad bonds. See my
                    telegram number 17 March 20th, 3 p.m., for amount deposited and full
                        report.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d158-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
